description:
scripts/moe-agent.ps1 still sends record_commit without `skipped`/`contested` on several paths that run after attribution:
- the failed sends (peel, build, gate, commit, ref contention, teardown);
- the Invoke-MoeRescueRef kind=rescue send;
- the catch/finally post-CAS committed re-sends.
sh's record_commit_rpc always reads ATTR_DIR/skipped and ATTR_DIR/contested, so on sh a held contested path still raises MOE_CONTESTED_HELD and its #governors alert on those outcomes, while on ps1 it raises nothing. Fix: merge Get-MoeRecordHeldFields (added by task-a2f243a1) into those sends where $attr is in scope. Add a postflight.{sh,ps1} assertion for at least one failed outcome.
